    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "This may be caused by the reinplace optimization. Under inductor, index_copy is lowered to index_put, and the reinplace.py further optimizes it into index_put_. However, the reinplace logic does not check whether the source and the destination tensors are the same, leading to an incorrect in-place transformation. As a result, this causes a read-write aliasing issue. If we add a check to skip such cases, the op remains as index_put, which internally performs a clone(), and the result remains consistent. Please feel free to correct me if I'm mistaken.\nhttps://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/178515d0ff6833c8e9221482b2a650ab31e00019/torch/_inductor/fx_passes/reinplace.py#L342-L350",
